    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.16), both of whom benefit from favorable park conditions and significant wind-aided boosts. **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a breakout day against Merrill Kelly, leveraging an elite SP_xERA of 5.37 and a strong platoon advantage, while **Jacob Wilson** profiles as our safest high-floor play, buoyed by a wind-out environment that elevates his power potential against Framber Valdez. Similarly, **Cole Carrigg** (70.41) projects as a premier start; while we are waiting on official lineup confirmation, his switch-hitting versatility and placement against Carson Whisenhunt\u2019s high-xERA (5.99) make him an essential component of our offensive strategy today.\n\nWhile we are deep in options, the decision to bench **Miguel Vargas** (42.35) was the most difficult call of the morning. Despite an elite xwOBA of 0.403, his matchup against a stifling 2.08 xERA arm in Sandoval suppressed his efficiency score just enough to keep him on the bench in favor of higher-projected bats. We are also exercising caution with **Gunnar Henderson** (69.47) and **Liam Hicks** (42.26); both face tough pitching assignments. **Gunnar Henderson** is battling a negative platoon edge against David Peterson, though his baseline talent keeps him in the \"Strong\" start tier. Conversely, **Liam Hicks** sits near our floor threshold; he is a risky play against a dominant 2.44 xERA arm like Brandon Miller. We are monitoring the status of **Heliot Ramos**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Cole Carrigg** closely, as their scores are contingent on assumed optimal batting order positions. If those lineup spots shift downward, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation.",
